2026-11-03T20:30:51.1603092Z    image gate: dent_house_1823_prairie album_1883: verdict "differs", 4 difference(s) open: the pavilion's crown: a pedimented attic front with its paired lights and finial standing between the slated cheeks of a steep crown; the build carries the pavilion's stone up a full-width attic under a coped gable, so its cheeks are stone where the vignette's are slate; the triple group's dormer: drawn broad with paired lights between scrolled consoles under a pediment that rises over the curb; the build's is K05's 2.0 m gabled dormer stopping under it; the arched opening under the landing: not built; the stack at the flank's rear corner, over the rear range: not built
2026-11-03T20:30:51.1609007Z    image gate: dent_house_1823_prairie chicagology_engraving: verdict "differs", 5 difference(s) open: the box bay's foot: the print corbels it out at about 1.8 m (y 895 px); the build carries it to grade 0.5 m proud: K08's corbelled oriel stands only on an upper floor, and the bay's 0.5 m is the least K08's window recesses fit in; the triple group's dormer: the print draws it broad, its carved pediment x 620-800 px rising to about 16.3 m (y 85 px), 1.3 m over the curb, between scrolled consoles; the build's is K05's paired-light gabled dormer at v 3.1 m, 2.0 m wide (K05's widest) and stopping under the curb; the stack at the north flank's rear (x 170-235 px), over the rear range, where K01 stands no stack: not built; the grilled round-arched basement doorway under the landing (x 925-975 px, y 935-990 px): not built; the narrow light beside the door on the principal storey (x 960-980 px, v 7.7-8.2 m): not built; the chamber storey's is laid at v 7.4 m
